# GAME PROJECT RESEARCH REFERENCE

When working on **game projects** (deckbuilders, roguelikes, Godot games, narrative games, or any other game repo):

1. **Consult `RESEARCH_ZERO_RUNTIME_GAMES_2026.md`** (reference-only content in the Project Starter rules pack, `starter/rules-pack/docs/`) when making decisions about:
   - Architecture (data-driven design, ECS, file size limits)
   - Build discipline (200–300 line max per Godot script)
   - Asset pipeline (LoRA, Suno, ElevenLabs)
   - Procedural generation patterns
   - Steam AI disclosure and legal

2. **Consult `AI_FIRST_BUILD_STRATEGY.md`** (same reference-only location) when making decisions about:
   - AI use by phase
   - Quality gates and human review

These are dated reference documents retained in the Project Starter pack — they are **not** installed into new projects automatically. Read them at the source (or copy one in deliberately if this project needs a local copy) before proposing architecture or build-discipline changes for game projects.
